Feature: Who may call the log store
  vmauth stands in front of VictoriaLogs, as VictoriaMetrics' guidance has it, and every client of the store reaches it through vmauth with a credential of its own: the collector may insert, Grafana, the route logs and the operator's recipes may query and load the interface, and no credential reaches deletion, storage administration or the store's own endpoints, nor vmauth's. vmauth sends the store's own credential with what it forwards, and Prometheus scrapes the store with it. Each credential is generated once in the cluster by External Secrets, and none is in a manifest, a values file, a command line or a log setting.

  One scenario needs a docker daemon, which the CI containers do not have: "The pinned vmauth in front of the pinned VictoriaLogs serves each client its own paths and refuses everything else". Its proof runs the store from the image its chart's render names and vmauth from the image the build names, each by its reference, in containers without network, without a capability, with a read-only root and a user that is not root, the store started with flags that require a credential, from a file the proof writes, and vmauth with the build's configuration, arguments and mounts and fresh credentials, and reads the status of each request a third container sends them. It runs with the other proofs of tests/log-store-access.bats wherever a docker daemon answers, on a developer's machine or an agent's, and skips, saying why, where none does, as under just ci and in CI, which run every other proof.

  Scenario: Each client of the log store addresses vmauth with a credential of its own from a Secret
    Given vmauth, the store, the collector, Grafana and the route logs as Flux builds them, Flux's substitution included, and their pinned charts rendered
    When each client's address and credential are read
    Then the collector's sink, Grafana's datasource and the route each address vmauth's Service on 8427, and no client addresses the store's Service but vmauth's url_prefix and the store's monitor; each presents its own user with a password taken from its own Secret by reference, the one vmauth reads for that user; the route's filter overwrites Authorization from vmauth-logs-route; and the collector and the route are applied only after vmauth, which waits for the store and its credential

  Scenario: vmauth gives the collector only the insert path and each reader only the query paths
    Given vmauth's configuration as its ConfigMap holds it
    When it is parsed and each user's paths are evaluated anchored, as vmauth matches them
    Then it holds the users vector, grafana, logs-route and operator and nothing else, each with a username, a password that is a placeholder of its own and a url_map alone, every entry of which sends to the store's Service and sets exactly the store's Authorization and the default tenant; the collector's one path is the bulk insert and each reader's are the interface's and the query paths; no reader's path matches a writer, the collector's matches no read, and no user's matches the root, deletion, storage administration, the store's or vmauth's own endpoints, the vmalert proxy or another writer's path

  Scenario: Every credential of the log store is generated in the cluster and appears in no manifest, argument or log setting
    Given vmauth, the store, the collector, Grafana and the route logs as Flux builds them, and their pinned charts and the Grafana operator's rendered
    When every Secret, password, credential, header value, environment entry and container argument is read
    Then no Secret is built or rendered; each of vmauth's placeholders is an environment entry from its non-optional Secret key and no entry has a value; each Secret is written once by an ExternalSecret from a Password generator of 64 hexadecimal digits, the route's and the operator's with their Basic value and the store's with its username and Basic value formed by the exact templates; every password, credential and header value is a placeholder or such a template; every container argument is free of a credential; vmauth logs no refused token and dumps no request, and the Grafana operator runs at its default log level

  Scenario: vmauth runs pinned and restricted, two replicas apart, with its own endpoints on a port it does not proxy
    Given vmauth as Flux builds it, the overlay, the Renovate records and the image's pin
    When its Kustomization, Deployment, Service, disruption budget and PodMonitor are read
    Then it is an application of monitoring that waits, after External Secrets, the store and the monitoring definitions; it runs the image pinned by tag and digest under the comment Renovate reads, in two replicas on different nodes, rolled one at a time with none unavailable and a budget that keeps one, restricted, with no token, a read-only root, requests and a memory limit; it proxies on 8427 alone, which the Service serves, and serves its health, its metrics and its keyed flags, profiles and reload on 8426, where its probes and its PodMonitor reach it and the Service does not

  Scenario: The store's scrape presents the store's credential and the store's pod is unchanged
    Given the store as Flux builds it and its pinned chart rendered with the tree's values and with them less the scrape's credential
    When its ServiceMonitor, its credential and its StatefulSet are read
    Then the monitor presents the username and password of victoria-logs-auth by Secret reference, which an ExternalSecret writes from a generator, the store's application waits for External Secrets, and the StatefulSet is byte for byte the one rendered without the credential, its probes unchanged

  Scenario: The pinned vmauth in front of the pinned VictoriaLogs serves each client its own paths and refuses everything else
    Given the store from the image its chart's render names, started with flags that require the store's credential, from a file the proof writes, and vmauth from the image the build names with the build's configuration, arguments and mounts and fresh credentials formed as the ExternalSecrets form them, side by side without network
    When requests are sent to vmauth's proxy port and its internal port with no credential, a wrong one and each user's
    Then the store so started refuses a request without that credential; vmauth refuses a request without a credential or with a wrong one, takes the collector's insert into the default tenant whatever tenant the client names, answers the operator's query with that line, refuses the collector's read as a missing route, every reader's insert and every user's request for deletion, storage administration, the store's and vmauth's own endpoints and the root, dot segments and doubled slashes included; serves each reader the interface, the build information and a query, the route's injected value included, and forwards each reader's request for the tenants' list, which the store refuses for the tenant vmauth names and lists when asked with none; and answers its health and metrics on its internal port without a credential and its flags, profiles and reload only with their keys
